{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can specify supplemental UI files to augment the UI bundle. These files are referred to collectively as the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "supplemental UI"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " because they supplement the files provided by the UI bundle."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The supplemental UI is useful for customizing an existing UI bundle without having to create a new one. It should not, however, be used as a replacement for developing a custom UI bundle. Rather, it should be used to make a few minor adjustments or additions to suit a particular environment. One such example is a favicon. Since the favicon is part of the brand identity, you may want to use an off-the-shelf UI bundle, but add your own favicon to it. You can use the supplemental UI to accomplish this goal."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The supplemental UI is overlaid onto the files in the loaded UI bundle. If the path of a file in the supplemental UI does not match the path of a file in the UI bundle, that file is added to the files from the UI bundle. If the path of a file in the supplemental UI matches the path of a file in the UI bundle, the file from the supplemental UI replaces the file from the UI bundle. The files in the supplemental UI are not otherwise processed."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "how-it-works",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "How it works"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The supplemental UI is configured using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "supplemental_files"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key under the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " category key. The key accepts either the path of a directory that contains the supplemental files or a map of virtual files. Currently, these two value types are mutually exclusive."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "If the value of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "supplemental_files"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key is a string, Antora assumes this value is the path of a directory. The value may be specified as a relative or absolute filesystem path. A relative path is expanded to an absolute path using the following rules:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "If the first path segment is a tilde ("
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "~"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "), the remaining path is resolved relative to the user’s home directory."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "If the first path segment is a dot ("
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "."
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "), the remaining path is resolved relative to the location of the playbook file."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "If the first path segment is a tilde directly followed by a plus sign ("
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "~+"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "), or does not begin with an aforementioned prefix, the remaining path is resolved relative to the current working directory."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": "ex-dir",
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui:\n  supplemental_files: ./supplemental-ui"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "yaml",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Antora scans this directory for files and adds them to the loaded UI bundle. The directory is assumed to be the root of the UI hierarchy. Therefore, the UI path is the path of the file relative to this directory."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Let’s assume you want to replace the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "head-meta"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": [
                      "path"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " partial with your own. Create the file at "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "supplemental-ui/partials/head-meta.hbs"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": [
                      "path"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " relative to the playbook file. Next, populate it with HTML and any optional template logic that you want to include."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "{{#with site.keys.googleSiteVerification}}\n<meta name=\"google-site-verification\" content=\"{{this}}\">\n{{/with}}"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "hbs",
                "roles": [],
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "supplemental-ui/partials/head-meta.hbs"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Antora will now use this partial in place of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "head-meta"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": [
                      "path"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " partial provided by the UI."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "directory",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Directory"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "As an alternative to a directory, you can specify the supplemental UI files directly in the playbook as virtual files. If the value of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "supplemental_files"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key is an array, Antora assumes that each entry is a virtual file. A virtual file entry consists of two keys, "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "path"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " and "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "contents"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ". The "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "path"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key is the relative path of the file in the UI (e.g., "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "partials/head-meta.hbs"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": [
                      "path"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "). The contents can be the specified directory or sourced from a file on the filesystem."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "If the value of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "contents"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key is a single line and ends with a file extension (e.g., "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ".hbs"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "), Antora assumes the value is the path of a file specified as a relative or absolute filesystem path. Otherwise, Antora uses the value as entered as the contents. If Antora determines the value is a file path, it reads the file and assigns the contents to the virtual file. If you omit the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "contents"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key, Antora will create an empty file."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Let’s assume you want to replace the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "head-meta"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": [
                      "path"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " partial with your own. You can define it as a virtual file in the playbook:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui:\n  supplemental_files:\n  - path: partials/head-meta.hbs\n    contents: |\n      {{#with site.keys.googleSiteVerification}}\n      <meta name=\"google-site-verification\" content=\"{{this}}\">\n      {{/with}}"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "yaml",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You could also put the contents in a file and reference it from the virtual file entry:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui:\n  supplemental_files:\n  - path: partials/head-meta.hbs\n    contents: ./supplemental-ui/partials/head-meta.hbs"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "yaml",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "If you are only defining a few small files, you can usually manage to define them directly in the playbook. If the files are larger, or you need to share them between multiple playbooks, its best to store them in separate files."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "virtual-files",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Virtual files"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "supplemental-files-key",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "supplemental_files key"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, publishable assets provided by the supplemental UI, such as images and JavaScript files, are published to the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "UI output directory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "ui-output-dir.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". It’s possible to configure certain files to be published to the root of the published site. These files are referred to as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "static files"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Static files are identified using the UI descriptor, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui.yml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", which also must be provided by the supplemental UI. The UI descriptor is a YAML file that configures certain aspects of the UI."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To create a static file, first create a file in the supplemental UI, typically outside of any of the standard folders. A good example of a static file is the favicon, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "favicon.ico"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", at the root of the site. Let’s assume you have put a favicon in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "supplemental-ui"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " directory. If you’re loading the supplemental UI from a path, add a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui.yml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " file with the following contents:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "static_files:\n- favicon.ico"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ui.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "static_files"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key accepts an array of strings. Each entry is the relative path to the file within the UI (it should not begin with a forward slash). Antora will pick up this file, see that the favicon is a static file, and publish it to the root of the site instead of the UI output directory."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you’re defining the supplemental UI as virtual files, you need to add an entry for both the favicon and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui.yml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " file."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ui:\n  supplemental_files:\n  - path: favicon.ico\n    contents: ./supplemental-ui/favicon.ico\n  - path: ui.yml\n    contents: |\n      static_files:\n      - favicon.ico"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the UI bundle contains a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ui.yml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " file, you will need to replicate its contents when redefining it for the supplemental UI. That’s because the file in the supplemental UI overwrites the file provided by the UI bundle."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "warning"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Although the supplemental UI provides a convenient way to add static files to the site, you may want to consider using an "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "extend:extensions.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " instead."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "static-files",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Static files"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Supplemental UI"
      }
    ]
  }
}
